sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Core mathematical functions—including retino_cortical_forward, retino_cortical_inverse, cortical_magnification_horton_hoyt, local_weight_coeff, lateral_weight_coeff, branch_growth, amplitude_gamma2, and amplitude_gamma3—carry clear docstrings citing the corresponding sections, equations, and figures in Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) and Horton and Hoyt (1991). Preset identifiers in PAPER_PRESETS and spec_to_preset also map directly to numbered figures in the 2001 and 2002 papers. Deduct 5 points because orientation_eigen_details truncates the Fourier series at max_harmonic = 4 (versus 10 in branch_coupling_sum) and clamps each harmonic coefficient to [-1.5, 1.5] via np.clip without citing where this heuristic originates. Deduct 5 points because _make_branch_candidate ranks branches using an undocumented potential score mode_count * (0.5 * lam * amp^2 + |eta| * amp^3 / 3 - 0.25 * denom * amp^4) not pinned to a published equation, and amplitude_gamma2/amplitude_gamma3 omit the sigmoid nonlinearity prefactors and linear resolvent of Eqs. 5.14-5.15 without comment. Deduct 4 points because planform_modes hardcodes arbitrary phase-drift multipliers (0.35, -0.25, -1.0, 0.5) and _eval_xy substitutes tanh(sharpness * max_phi |val|) for Bressloff's oriented contour rendering without tracing these approximations to rust-v1-sim. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L389–L470: Equation-pinned implementations of local_weight_coeff (Eq. 3.12), lateral_weight_coeff (Eq. 4.9), and branch_growth (Section 4, Figs. 16-17). <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L389-L470>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L480–L507: Unexplained [-1.5, 1.5] np.clip bound and max_harmonic = 4 truncation in orientation_eigen_details. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L480-L507>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L553–L592: Heuristic branch-selection score formula in _make_branch_candidate without an equation citation. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L553-L592>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L759–L850: Hardcoded phase-drift multipliers in planform_modes and max-over-orientation tanh rendering in _eval_xy. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L759-L850>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Code-to-model traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

